9, 2019. He quit smoking on February 3, 2024, and his disclosure regarding his tobacco use was honest. There is no documented history of alcohol consumption during the provided visits.\n\n• **Family History:** \nJames' mother has a documented history of type 2 diabetes, diagnosed at the age of 73 and currently living at the age of 90. This family history is relevant in the context of potential genetic predispositions for metabolic conditions.\n\n• **Additional Findings:** \nDuring the annual physical examination on August 20, 2023, all routine laboratory tests were within normal limits, and no additional significant"
